<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchDaemon for the DNSwitch engine, registered via SMAppService (docs/07 §1/§4).

  - Label MUST equal this file's name without ".plist" and is the plistName the
    app passes to SMAppService.daemon(plistName:).
  - BundleProgram is a path RELATIVE to the app bundle root; the engine binary is
    dropped there by the Xcode Run-Script phase before code signing.
  - KeepAlive={SuccessfulExit:false}: relaunch only on a crash (non-zero exit);
    a clean signal-driven exit(0) after DNS restore is respected, not relaunched.
  - RunAtLoad: come up at boot (the engine self-tests + gates its own pin, BL-1).
  - Umask=63 (0o77): launchd creates StandardErrorPath BEFORE exec, so this is
    the only way to have the log be 0600 root:wheel from its very first byte —
    no window, and it covers what no log handler can (Go runtime panics, dyld,
    launchd's own job errors all write straight to fd 2). The engine resets its
    own umask to 0o022 as the first statement of main(), because 0o77 would
    otherwise be inherited by the networksetup children and could clamp shared
    system files. Deliberately NOT a path change: pointing StandardErrorPath
    into /var/db/dnswitch looked tidier but launchd creates missing parent
    directories as 0744, which on a fresh install would REPLACE the 0700
    snapshot directory with a world-readable one.
    NOTE: this key only reaches launchd on a FRESH registration. An
    SMAppService daemon keeps the plist launchd cached when the bundle was
    registered, and register() on an already-enabled service does not re-read
    it (measured: launchctl print still reported the previous bundle version).
    engine/logperm_darwin.go clamps the descriptor at startup to cover
    upgrades; the two together leave no case uncovered.
  - ExitTimeOut: bound BL-A cleanup on reboot; sized above one wedged
    networksetup call (15s) so a live `launchctl bootout` restore isn't
    SIGKILLed mid-way. A stuck restore is still repaired by next-boot reconcile.
  - EnvironmentVariables/PATH: launchd gives no login PATH; the engine also uses
    an absolute networksetup path, so this is belt-and-suspenders.
  - AssociatedBundleIdentifiers: makes the item show as "DNSwitch" (not the bare
    Label) in System Settings › Login Items, matching the app's approval prompt.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.fx.dnswitch.engine</string>

	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/MacOS/dnswitch-engine</string>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>

	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<dict>
		<key>SuccessfulExit</key>
		<false/>
	</dict>

	<key>ExitTimeOut</key>
	<integer>25</integer>

	<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
	<dict>
		<key>PATH</key>
		<string>/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/bin:/sbin</string>
	</dict>

	<key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>com.fx.dnswitch</string>
	</array>

	<key>Umask</key>
	<integer>63</integer>

	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/var/log/com.fx.dnswitch.engine.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
